WEBVTT

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.820
<i>Tron has sworn revenge on all his opponents.</i>

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.550
<i>Then, there is the dad of Kaito and Haruto, Dr. Faker.</i>

00:00:07.380 --> 00:00:12.160
<i>His goal is to ally himself with the Varian World, to become the ruler of this world!</i>

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:16.150
<i>I won't forgive him for forcing Kaito to collect Numbers for that reason!</i>

00:00:16.900 --> 00:00:21.130
<i>To teach these egoistical adults a lesson, I will definitely win this!</i>

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:25.550
<i>I will become Duel Champion!
 I'll bring it to 'em!</i>

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:30.910
<i>The Semi-Finals of the World Duel Carnival!</i>

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:35.110
<i>The battlefield for our passionate Duelists...is here!</i>

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:38.510
<i>Show yourself, Duel Tower!</i>

00:01:05.620 --> 00:01:08.060
<i>On these sky piercing Duel Fields,</i>

00:01:08.660 --> 00:01:12.630
<i>our warriors will clash and fight to their hearts' content!</i>

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.390
Ao Yuma's opponent is Shark.

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:19.120
This could be a slight advantage for Yuma,

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:21.530
because he has been fighting Shark several times already.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:25.250
To summarize, he should know his abilities.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:27.630
But the same goes for his opponent.

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:32.550
Besides, Yuma does tend to forget the skills of his opponents.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:37.050
Meowhat? Whose side are you on, Tokunosuke?!

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.920
<i>Sure, Yuma has fought against him many times...</i>

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.450
<i>But that Monster Shark received during his fight against IV...</i>

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.130
<i>In order to complete my revenge, I am willing to accept everything!</i>

00:01:54.130 --> 00:01:56.920
<i>Come, Shark Drake!</i>

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.470
<i>Accept my wish, and evolve!</i>

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:04.890
<i>Show yourself, Chaos Number 32!</i>

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:10.310
<i>Marine Biting Dragon - Shark Drake Vice!</i>

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:13.560
Yuma...

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.220
Be careful...

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.840
<i>Now, finally, the first round of the Semi-Finals will start!</i>

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:25.630
<i>Practically unknown until this competition, in this tournament he has won many hard fights!</i>

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:30.070
<i>The wonder of the tournament finals! The miracle-boy who managed to pull through!</i>

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:32.170
<i>Yuma Tsukumo!</i>

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:37.120
Thanks, thanks- oops!

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:44.720
<i>On the other side, out of the depths of exile from the Dueling stage because of a scandal,</i>

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.880
<i>he has reemerged again as a hero:</i>

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.920
<i>The revenger!</i>

00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:58.730
Today we will settle this!

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.210
Somehow Shark is very odd...

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.310
Hey, Shark! Shark!

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.830
What's wrong with the guy?

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:17.600
<i>Now, my two heroes, up to the stage for the final battle!</i>

00:03:25.540 --> 00:03:29.930
<i>Only one will earn the invitation to move on past this field of the Semi-Finals!</i>

00:03:30.660 --> 00:03:32.560
<i>Now, who will survive to the finals?</i>

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:35.490
<i>Will it be Yuma?! Or Ryoga?!</i>

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.950
<i>Let yourself be emblazoned by this fiery battle!</i>

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:43.200
<i>Heart Burning!</i>

00:03:43.970 --> 00:03:49.020
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:54.360
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:04:07.210 --> 00:04:11.210
<i>Hey, my friends, what scenery do you suppose</i>

00:04:12.340 --> 00:04:17.010
<i>awaits us on the other side of this hill?</i>

00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:21.600
<i>Hey, my friends, let's climb it together</i>

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:27.640
<i>It's too late for us to turn back now</i>

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:32.730
<i>The time has come to combine
 together the power dwelling inside me</i>

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:38.280
<i>Gotta release my Soul Drive</i>

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:44.080
<i>Advance, advance, beyond the limits of your strength</i>

00:04:44.290 --> 00:04:49.120
<i>Come along with me and burn our flame of life</i>

00:04:49.670 --> 00:04:54.590
<i>Keep running, keep running, until you get there</i>

00:04:54.920 --> 00:05:00.260
<i>Once again, once again, keep those challenges coming</i>

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:06.430
<i>My friends, keep on living in the here and now</i>

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:12.520
<i>Keep pressing onward together no matter what happens</i>

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:24.090
"Number 62: The Vanishing Bond!
 Yuma VS Shark: The Fated Duel!!"

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:24.970
Really... What's up with Shark?

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.300
I can't believe this... The darkness of the Number...

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:28.930
Huh?

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.850
During his fight against IV, Shark suddenly received that Chaos Number...

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:40.820
This could only happen because the dark powers of the Number took absolute control of him.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:43.400
Shark...

00:05:45.610 --> 00:05:48.240
What kind of fight will you show me?

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:51.080
I'm really looking forward to this, you know.

00:05:51.700 --> 00:05:55.080
Though it's already obvious who the winner will be.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.790
Snap out of it, Shark! Hey!

00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:03.460
Shark!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:05.800
Yuma.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.760
If he really is possessed by the Number,

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.850
Then his battle instincts should be sharpened as well.

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.350
Don't let your guard down.

00:06:15.850 --> 00:06:16.270
Sure.

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:19.440
Then, I'll have to get through to him with the Duel!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:21.230
Let's go!

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:25.740
Duel Disk, set!

00:06:30.570 --> 00:06:32.780
D-Gazer, set!

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:35.700
Duel Target: Lock-on!

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:38.210
<i>AR Vision: Link established.</i>

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.380
Duel!!

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.340
I will go first!

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.550
My turn, draw!

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:49.630
I set a Monster in Dace-Down Defense Mode!

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:55.680
Then I set a card and end my turn!

00:06:56.640 --> 00:07:01.690
Right. Set in Dace-Down Defense Mode is Dododo Bot with 1900 Defense Points.

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.190
The other set card is the Trap Card, Attack Invulnerability.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:10.490
With this, there is a high possibility that we'll survive the first attack.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:12.370
Come on, Shark!

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.830
My turn. Draw.

00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:19.580
I Summon Spear Shark!

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:27.840
1600 Attack Points! If that's all...

00:07:28.340 --> 00:07:31.630
Stay wary! Shark's Dueling isn't that simple.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:35.390
Spear Shark attacks the Face-Down Defense Monster.

00:07:35.720 --> 00:07:36.310
What?!

00:07:36.970 --> 00:07:40.810
Without any precautions...  he is attacking Dododo Bot?

00:07:51.740 --> 00:07:52.780
Shark?!

00:07:59.540 --> 00:08:00.790
I can't believe this...

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.040
He is attacking without any precautions...

00:08:05.130 --> 00:08:07.630
<i>What's up with Ryoga Kamishiro?!</i>

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:12.760
<i>Because of this careless attack, he will receive the damage!</i>

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:14.970
I've never seen Shark act like that.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:18.640
The guy's Dueling as bad as Yuma used to.

00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.100
No... This may be part of his strategy.

00:08:21.810 --> 00:08:26.520
To summarize, maybe Shark wants to show Yuma-<i>kun</i> up with this,

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.400
as their Dueling patterns are completely reversed.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:33.240
Then you're saying he took the damage on purpose?

00:08:33.530 --> 00:08:34.570
To do such a thing...

00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:40.200
<i>I set one card face-down and end my turn.</i>

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:46.880
Shark...You've always had such harsh fighting spirit, but now this?

00:08:47.630 --> 00:08:51.380
Just what is going on in his head?

00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:57.220
Stay cautious anyway, and pay attention to that set card.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.350
Ha, you betcha!

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:02.980
Let's go! My turn! Draw!

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:05.900
I Summon Gogogo Golem!

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:14.110
Then I change Dododo Bot to Attack Position!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:18.740
Yuma!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:23.620
Go, Gogogo Golem! Attack Spear Shark!

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:35.300
Shark!

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:42.470
Still not back to your senses?

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:45.350
Then with a Direct Attack.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.100
Go, Dododo Bot!

00:09:48.560 --> 00:09:50.230
Thunder Blade!!

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.280
<i>This is intense!</i>

00:10:01.870 --> 00:10:05.250
<i>He received 1800 damage with one blow!</i>

00:10:07.000 --> 00:10:09.580
<i>Hurry and get up, Ryoga!</i>

00:10:10.330 --> 00:10:11.540
Get up, Shark!

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:13.670
Come at me like you always did!

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:20.430
Shark! Shark! Shark! Shark!

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.600
That Shark... This is really disappointing.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.560
What are you waiting for, Shark?! Stand up already!

00:10:30.020 --> 00:10:33.650
Haven't you always bitten back no matter how strong your opponent was?!

00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:35.940
That's the Shark I know!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:38.490
A shark that won't fight back is no shark!

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.330
But we aren't finished yet.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:51.920
I set one card and end my turn!

00:10:53.540 --> 00:10:54.710
Go on and take your turn!

00:10:55.380 --> 00:10:58.380
Shark, get up! Will you get up, Shark?!

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:03.010
<i>Right... I'm here to Duel.</i>

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:06.430
<i>But... Why am I fighting?</i>

00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:11.100
<i>What am I fighting for?</i>

00:11:12.730 --> 00:11:15.940
<i>I can't remember... Why... Just why?</i>

00:11:17.230 --> 00:11:18.360
<i>Did you forget?</i>

00:11:20.610 --> 00:11:21.200
<i>Tron...</i>

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:24.870
<i>Thank God you didn't forget me.</i>

00:11:25.490 --> 00:11:28.750
<i>It seems like something of your self still remains.</i>

00:11:29.580 --> 00:11:30.660
<i>But it's all right.</i>

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.460
<i>If you listen to what I will tell you, you will Duel without hesitation.</i>

00:11:35.790 --> 00:11:38.590
<i>Well? Then, why are you fighting?</i>

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:42.090
<i>You see... It's for </i>me<i>.</i>

00:11:42.590 --> 00:11:43.590
<i>For you?</i>

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:44.720
<i>Yes.</i>

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:49.230
<i>You will fight in my place, as my marionette.</i>

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:51.640
<i>So, the opponent you have to defeat is...</i>

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.900
<i>My... opponent I have to defeat... is...</i>

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.000
Shark!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:21.420
What's up, Shark!?

00:12:21.840 --> 00:12:23.720
<i>Oh my, what is happening here?</i>

00:12:24.130 --> 00:12:26.850
<i>Suddenly Ryoga seems to be suffering from heavy pain!</i>

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.180
Now, we can't have this...

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:33.770
You still can't remember the opponent you have to defeat?

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.610
Even though I explained it that nicely yesterday...

00:12:39.150 --> 00:12:42.860
All right. Then I will explain it once again.

00:12:43.990 --> 00:12:45.740
The one you have to defeat is...

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:53.660
<i>Rio...</i>

00:12:57.330 --> 00:12:57.750
<i>IV...</i>

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:04.220
<i>Tron?!</i>

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:09.220
<i>The one I have to defeat is Tron?!</i>

00:13:10.510 --> 00:13:12.390
<i>Who is that guy?</i>

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:16.480
<i>This is Dr. Faker.</i>

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:20.020
<i>Faker? Faker...</i>

00:13:20.860 --> 00:13:24.820
<i>That name... I do remember, I seemed to have heard it somewhere...</i>

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.620
<i>Rio!</i>

00:13:37.170 --> 00:13:38.460
<i>Dr. Faker.</i>

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:42.210
<i>Of course you heard that name before.</i>

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:46.090
<i>I mean, you've been hunting the guy down all this time.</i>

00:13:46.930 --> 00:13:49.930
<i>After Dr. Faker made your sister suffer so terribly,</i>

00:13:49.930 --> 00:13:52.470
<i>you swore in your heart to take revenge.</i>

00:13:52.970 --> 00:13:55.390
<i>Right... That's right...</i>

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:59.310
<i>Rio had to suffer because of Dr. Faker!</i>

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:02.900
<i>My true enemy is...</i>

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:05.780
<i>Right.</i>

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:09.620
<i>Dr. Faker... And wasn't there someone else?</i>

00:14:10.530 --> 00:14:12.910
<i>That annoying guy, who always gets in your way?</i>

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:14.410
<i>Someone else...</i>

00:14:25.420 --> 00:14:27.090
<i>Yuma Tsukumo!</i>

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:32.680
<i>Right! Didn't you always think of him as an eyesore?</i>

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:36.390
<i>He always was bothering and in your way, with everything you did.</i>

00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:40.600
<i>And he now stands right before you.</i>

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:44.650
<i>He teamed up with Dr. Faker.</i>

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:49.610
From those who made your sister suffer that terribly, one half is over there.

00:14:53.580 --> 00:14:54.790
Shark!

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:58.790
I'll never forgive you, Yuma!

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.460
You... Because of you...!

00:15:06.880 --> 00:15:07.340
Yuma.

00:15:08.050 --> 00:15:08.510
This is...?!

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.510
It's the same crest as Tron's.

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:18.060
So Shark's not only being controlled by the Number, but by Tron as well?!

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:20.140
Well, you could say that.

00:15:20.770 --> 00:15:26.190
To be precise, my faithful servant, the Number, has united with him.

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:30.860
Ryoga has now become my absolutely faithful, darling puppet.

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:34.370
Now tear Yuma Tsukumo apart!

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:38.750
Let's go! My turn! Draw!

00:15:39.120 --> 00:15:41.620
I Summon Two-Head Shark!

00:15:44.750 --> 00:15:48.920
Then, from my hand, I activate the Magic Card, Aqua Jet!

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:54.010
Until the end of the turn, the Attack Power of Two-Head Shark will be increased by 1000!

00:15:54.720 --> 00:15:56.510
Attack Gogogo Golem!

00:15:58.020 --> 00:15:59.430
Defend! Yuma!

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.350
Trap, activate! Attack Invulnerability!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:07.190
With its effect, Gogogo Golem won't be destroyed!

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:12.570
Naive! I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Shark Spark, from my hand!

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:15.200
When this card is sent to the Graveyard,

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:17.660
it negates an opponent's Trap!

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:18.410
What?!

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:26.130
Resume the attack, Two-Head Shark!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:37.680
Yuma!

00:16:38.100 --> 00:16:38.810
That's not all!

00:16:39.260 --> 00:16:41.930
Two-Head Shark can attack twice per turn!

00:16:42.230 --> 00:16:43.850
Attack Dododo Bot!

00:16:52.820 --> 00:16:55.160
Shark! You're so cool!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:57.070
Shark! You're hot!

00:16:57.120 --> 00:16:59.790
<i>Until a moment ago, it looked like Ryoga had surrendered,</i>

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:02.540
<i>but now he managed a furious counterattack reverse!</i>

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:06.710
<i>Now everyone's got their Heart... Burning!</i>

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.540
What a sudden change of personality!

00:17:08.710 --> 00:17:10.090
What just happened up there?

00:17:10.210 --> 00:17:11.760
Treacherous like a cat!

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:15.430
Does this guy want to be put down...? <i>Meouw</i>!

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:19.850
Wh... why?

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.560
I'm not finished yet!

00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:26.770
Then I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Dead Sweep, from my hand!

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:29.480
When an opponent's Monster was destroyed by battle,

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:34.280
the Attack Power of one Water-Attribute Monster in my Graveyard is decreased by 1000 points and it is Special Summoned!

00:17:34.740 --> 00:17:37.160
I bring back Spear Shark!

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:40.450
Sick him, Spear Shark!

00:17:43.500 --> 00:17:46.210
This is the payback for my little sister!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:46.830
Huh?

00:17:47.460 --> 00:17:49.920
Direct attack Yuma!

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:57.760
Yuma!

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:01.890
Shark's incredible when he finally gets serious.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:04.020
No... This is much more than serious.

00:18:04.730 --> 00:18:07.230
Now Shark is being controlled by Tron.

00:18:07.690 --> 00:18:11.940
I am positive that this is where his current strength is coming from.

00:18:12.480 --> 00:18:15.320
Under Tron's control...? And now, he is...?!

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:18.360
<i>I will never forgive you, Yuma!</i>

00:18:18.360 --> 00:18:20.870
<i>This is the payback for my little sister!</i>

00:18:21.240 --> 00:18:25.950
Im- impossible! It can't be that Tron manipulated his memories?

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:29.880
That's right, like he did during your Duel with III,

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:31.630
this likely happened to Shark as well...

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.760
I set one card and end my turn!

00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:39.760
The Attack Power of Two-Head Shark is decreased by 1000.

00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:43.180
Awesome! So awesome!

00:18:43.430 --> 00:18:48.060
He instantly defeated the two Monsters of the opponent, and on top of that made a direct attack!

00:18:48.310 --> 00:18:50.520
I expected no less from the man I set my eyes on!

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:55.440
Now he is flawlessly Dr. Faker's assassin!

00:18:58.320 --> 00:19:00.910
I have to save Shark from Tron somehow,

00:19:01.490 --> 00:19:02.490
but what should I do?

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:04.330
It's not only Tron.

00:19:04.620 --> 00:19:07.290
There is still the Number inside Shark's heart.

00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:12.460
Additionally, it has already evolved into a Chaos Number, Shark Drake Vice!

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:17.840
If Shark manages to Summon the Number before we break the curse of Tron...

00:19:18.220 --> 00:19:21.430
I know! I just have to win this Duel, right?

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:24.680
I'll win and wake Shark up!

00:19:24.970 --> 00:19:30.690
Yuma! Yuma! Yuma! Yuma!

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:32.940
My turn! Draw!

00:19:33.860 --> 00:19:35.730
I Summon Gogogo Ghost!

00:19:47.290 --> 00:19:51.420
Go, Gogogo Ghost! Attack Spear Shark!

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.540
Trap, activate! Zeus' Breath!

00:19:57.420 --> 00:20:00.800
This card can negate my opponent's Monster's attack,

00:20:01.340 --> 00:20:05.010
and when there is a Water-Attribute Monster on my field,

00:20:05.260 --> 00:20:07.810
it can inflict 800 damage to my opponent!

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.190
He had a Trap like that?!

00:20:12.560 --> 00:20:14.480
Shark really is flawless!

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:17.190
Now Yuma-<i>kun</i> only has 1800 of his Life left!

00:20:17.860 --> 00:20:19.940
But Shark only has 1700 left...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.490
The real match has only get started!

00:20:23.070 --> 00:20:26.200
I set one card.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:28.030
Turn end!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.910
It's over, Yuma!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:36.790
You have nothing left to defeat me.

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:40.050
I'm going to pay you back for my sister's suffering and get my revenge!

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:43.050
It wasn't me! Open your eyes, Shark!

00:20:43.470 --> 00:20:45.760
The one who hurt your sister is Tron!

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:51.770
You're trying to make up excuses now, pleading for your life?

00:20:52.730 --> 00:20:56.230
Unforgivable! For this, I will send you right to Hell!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.190
With my own hands and my Number!

00:20:59.980 --> 00:21:00.820
Your Number?!

00:21:01.230 --> 00:21:05.700
That's bad! There are already 2 Level Four Monsters on Shark's field.

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:09.580
My turn! Draw!

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:12.410
I Summon Sharktopus!

00:21:19.040 --> 00:21:25.470
I Overlay the three Level Four Monsters: Spear Shark, Twin-head Shark, and Sharktopus!

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:32.310
I use these three Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:34.430
Xyz Summon!

00:21:35.940 --> 00:21:38.860
Show yourself, Number 32!

00:21:40.690 --> 00:21:43.610
Marine Biting Dragon - Shark Drake!

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:55.080
He's finally...

00:21:58.210 --> 00:22:00.790
Nice. Very nice, Ryouga.

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:04.840
Go on and bury that annoying Yuma Tsukumo alive!

00:22:10.600 --> 00:22:15.770
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:22:16.020 --> 00:22:21.400
<i>Move on ahead, speeding up our throbbing beats</i>

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:32.080
<i>Listen boys and girls, here's the secret to boys and girls like you</i>

00:22:32.450 --> 00:22:36.330
<i>You're really just so spontaneous, wild as can be</i>

00:22:36.330 --> 00:22:37.620
<i>I bet you didn't know?</i>

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:40.330
<i>You might be a handful, but what's wrong with that?</i>

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.960
<i>Be up to no good, but learn for real</i>

00:22:43.130 --> 00:22:48.170
<i>Go the unpredictable route and shuffle your cards with a goal in mind</i>

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:53.510
<i>Whenever you feel like you've lost your way, just take a minute to close your eyes...</i>

00:22:53.640 --> 00:22:59.140
<i>Shout "stop!" with all you've got, and there's your boundary line.</i>

00:23:00.520 --> 00:23:05.650
<i>We stand tall, until we have victory in our grasp</i>

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:11.110
<i>We won't just stop here, not when we don't want to have any regrets.</i>

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:16.370
<i>Even if we get hurt, we can't just hesitate now</i>

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:22.000
<i>We won't just give up, not when our future's a lot brighter than our today</i>

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:27.210
<i>Seriousness... It'll only make us keep fighting even harder</i>

00:23:27.420 --> 00:23:32.720
<i>We'll always get as fascinated as we want, and we'll fight on every day</i>

00:23:41.650 --> 00:23:46.150
Shark was restrained by Tron's curse. Just what should I do to bring him back to his senses?

00:23:46.690 --> 00:23:49.110
I can no longer endure the agony of losing friends!

00:23:49.490 --> 00:23:51.240
It's coming! The Chaos Number!

00:23:51.660 --> 00:23:54.120
I will save you using whatever method possible!

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:56.620
This is bad! At this rate, Yuma will...

00:23:57.080 --> 00:23:59.410
Shark or Astral... I can only choose one of them?

00:24:00.370 --> 00:24:02.000
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:05.040
"Shark's Back!
 The Bonds Bounded By Bringin' it to 'Em!"

00:24:05.920 --> 00:24:08.340
I'm going to bring your real heart back!

00:24:11.300 --> 00:24:13.840
Yuma, you're still playing with Shark?

00:24:14.140 --> 00:24:17.890
Shark and me are now 1:1, so I'm at 50%! I won't lose this!

00:24:18.350 --> 00:24:20.680
Even I'm not sure who will win this.

00:24:20.680 --> 00:24:23.100
After all, this is a battle between a horse and a shark.

00:24:21.270 --> 00:24:24.900
"Yuma VS Shark"
 "Uma (Horse) VS Shark"

00:24:23.440 --> 00:24:24.310
<i>That's</i> your problem?!
